# `bin/*` rather than `bin/`: git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT
# DIRECTORY is excluded, so the negation below is silently inert under the
# directory form — which is how the first attempt at this fix still left the
# guard untracked.
bin/*
# …except the sandbox guard, which is SOURCE that happens to live in bin/.
# bin/ is ignored because it is where build output lands, and that rule silently
# swallowed bin/blast-radius on the commit that introduced it: `git add -A` skipped
# it, `git status` stayed clean, and CI was the first thing to notice the file
# every agent instruction points at did not exist in the repo. TestTheGuardIsTracked
# is what makes that unrepeatable.
!bin/blast-radius

# Working documents: implementation plans, review write-ups, red-team round
# reports, buildable specs. One committed design document per subject lives in
# .claude/design/; the process that got there does not.
#
# Ignored rather than merely untracked, and that is the point: these files were
# once removed with `git rm --cached` and a later `git add -A` in the same
# session put every one of them straight back, including a plan that had been
# deliberately untracked from the day it was written. An instruction a command
# can quietly undo is not a rule.
.claude/scratchpad/

# Agent worktrees. Same reason, one level up: a `git add -A` committed one as an
# embedded gitlink, which is a pointer to a commit the clone cannot resolve.
.claude/worktrees/

# Real profiles used to test snug against real accounts on this machine. They
# name host paths, host account names and host key files, so they are local by
# construction — symlink one into $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/snug/profiles.d to use it.
# Ignored rather than untracked for the reason above it.
local-profiles/

# Throwaway code that answers a question by execution. poc/nsd was committed and
# then sat unbuilt for a milestone: its own Go module, so `./...`, `go vet` and
# `make gate` never saw it — while one of its harnesses built ./cmd/snug and
# grepped internal/policy for a literal sentence. Keep such a thing locally if it
# is useful; the measurements belong in .claude/design/ and the code does not
# belong in a clone. Ignored rather than merely untracked for the reason the
# .claude/scratchpad/ entry above gives.
poc/
.integration-*.log

# internal/cli's dry-run fixture tree. testTree builds it under
# $SNUG_TEST_FIXTURE_ROOT, $HOME or $XDG_CACHE_HOME and never inside the
# checkout, so this entry should match nothing — it is here because one WAS
# found under internal/cli/ and had to be rm -rf'd out of a worktree before
# committing. The cleanup is a t.Cleanup, which does not survive a panic, a
# -timeout kill or an interrupted run, and a leftover under the module root also
# races the source sweeps in internal/policy (issue #350). An instruction a
# routine `git add -A` can quietly undo is not a rule.
snug-dryrun-fixture-*/
.engine-store/

# scripts/pid-nesting.py's handshake file. It lands in the SANDBOX's working
# directory, which is this checkout whenever the target is the repository
# itself — the one place a payload can write that the host side can also read.
BWRAP_PID
